00:19:13,236 --> 00:19:17,239
See, they start to turn,
but they never take the final step.

243
00:19:17,406 --> 00:19:19,741
-Really?
-See, if they never eat human flesh...

244
00:19:19,909 --> 00:19:22,577
-...they don't fully transform.
-Go vegan, stay human?

245
00:19:22,745 --> 00:19:26,915
Basically. Or, in this case,
eat a lot of raw meat, just not--

246
00:19:27,083 --> 00:19:28,416
-Long pig.
-Right.

247
00:19:31,295 --> 00:19:34,256
Good on you
for the due diligence, Sam.

248
00:19:34,423 --> 00:19:36,258
But those are fairy tales.

249
00:19:37,426 --> 00:19:41,221
The fact is,
every Rougarou I ever saw or heard of...

250
00:19:42,098 --> 00:19:43,139
...took that bite.

251
00:19:43,307 --> 00:19:45,767
Okay, well,
that doesn't mean that Jack will.

252
00:19:45,935 --> 00:19:49,396
So, what do we do? Sit and hope,
and wait for a body count?

253
00:19:49,564 --> 00:19:52,232
No, we talk to him.
Explain what's happening.

254
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:55,735
-That way, he can fight it.
-Fight it?

255
00:19:55,903 --> 00:19:57,571
Are you kidding me?

256
00:19:59,323 --> 00:20:03,660
You ever been really hungry?
I mean, haven't-eaten-in-days hungry?

257
00:20:03,828 --> 00:20:05,328
Yeah.

258
00:20:05,538 --> 00:20:06,955
Right, then.

259
00:20:07,123 --> 00:20:11,334
So somebody slaps a big, juicy sirloin
in front of you, you walking away?

260
00:20:13,045 --> 00:20:16,798
That's what we are to him now.
Meat on legs.

261
00:20:17,633 --> 00:20:19,968
I'm sorry.
I'm sure he's a stand-up guy.

262
00:20:20,136 --> 00:20:23,179
But it's pure, base instinct.
Everything in nature's gotta eat.

263
00:20:23,347 --> 00:20:25,640
You think he can stop himself
because he's nice?

264
00:20:25,808 --> 00:20:27,809
I don't know.
We're not gonna kill him...

265
00:20:27,977 --> 00:20:31,813
...unless he does something
to get killed for.

266
00:20:41,866 --> 00:20:44,117
What's up with your brother?

267
00:20:44,994 --> 00:20:46,828
Don't get me started.

268
00:20:56,130 --> 00:20:58,006
Oh, God.

269
00:20:58,591 --> 00:20:59,633
You scared me.

270
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:01,885
I'm sorry.
I didn't mean to sneak up on you.

271
00:21:02,845 --> 00:21:04,721
How are you feeling?

272
00:21:06,849 --> 00:21:08,516
I'm feeling pissed, Jack.

273
00:21:10,895 --> 00:21:15,649
I had to drive myself to the hospital
last night. I was there until 2.

274
00:21:15,816 --> 00:21:17,192
I'm so sorry.

275
00:21:17,360 --> 00:21:19,194
-What happened?
-l don't know.

276
00:21:19,362 --> 00:21:24,032
I saw your blood, and I got dizzy,
and l just had to get out.

277
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:26,534
You could've called.
I left you a dozen messages.

278
00:21:26,702 --> 00:21:27,702
I know. My phone died.

279
00:21:27,870 --> 00:21:31,373
I couldn't find a pay phone. I....
It was a mess.

280
00:21:32,375 --> 00:21:35,710
But l am sorry.

281
00:21:38,381 --> 00:21:42,217
And l promise
it won't ever happen again.

282
00:21:43,219 --> 00:21:44,260
And certainly...

283
00:21:45,638 --> 00:21:49,057
...not to a wife as stunning as you.

284
00:21:50,351 --> 00:21:52,352
Better not.

285
00:21:54,397 --> 00:21:58,233
I swear, you know, one little cut....

286
00:21:58,401 --> 00:22:01,695
You know,
blood's never bothered you before.

287
00:22:02,905 --> 00:22:04,572
Well...

288
00:22:05,032 --> 00:22:06,533
...l've changed.

289
00:22:08,911 --> 00:22:11,246
This doesn't get you off the hook,
you know.

290
00:22:11,414 --> 00:22:15,583
No, no. Think diamonds.
Think Kobe-size.

291
00:22:24,927 --> 00:22:28,430
-What has gotten into you?
-l don't know.

292
00:22:30,933 --> 00:22:33,768
Hey, Jack, just slow down.

293
00:22:34,478 --> 00:22:37,939
Jack. Jack, I mean it, stop.

294
00:22:38,107 --> 00:22:39,441
Jack. Ow!

295
00:22:39,608 --> 00:22:43,570
Jack, stop! Stop it! Stop it!

296
00:22:45,740 --> 00:22:49,242
-You son of a bitch.
-l'm sorry.

297
00:22:50,202 --> 00:22:52,620
What the hell is wrong with you?

298
00:22:53,456 --> 00:22:58,460
I don't know.

299
00:23:01,922 --> 00:23:05,133
We're gonna go have a little chat
with this guy, which, you know...

300
00:23:05,301 --> 00:23:06,843
...l'm down.

301
00:23:07,011 --> 00:23:10,764
I just wanna make sure, if push comes,
you're gonna shove.

302
00:23:12,308 --> 00:23:13,475
-Meaning?
-Odds are...

303
00:23:13,642 --> 00:23:15,935
...we're gonna have to burn
this guy alive.

304
00:23:16,103 --> 00:23:18,354
This guy has a name and a wife.

305
00:23:18,522 --> 00:23:21,816
Yeah, who we're probably gonna make
a widow, okay? You heard Travis.

306
00:23:21,984 --> 00:23:24,486
-He's gonna turn. They always turn.
-Maybe he won't.

307
00:23:24,653 --> 00:23:28,031
-Maybe he can fight it off.
-Maybe he can't. That's all I'm saying.

308
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:31,659
-We'll just have to see, then, okay?
-See, this is what l mean, Sam.

309
00:23:31,827 --> 00:23:34,829
You sure your emotions
aren't getting in the way here?

310
00:23:35,498 --> 00:23:37,248
What are you talking about?

311
00:23:38,501 --> 00:23:42,295
You know, nice dude,
but he's got something evil inside him.

312
00:23:42,463 --> 00:23:44,798
Something in his blood.
Maybe you can relate.

313
00:23:46,759 --> 00:23:47,842
Stop the car.

314
00:23:48,010 --> 00:23:51,179
-What?
-Stop the car, or I will.

315
00:24:01,273 --> 00:24:04,359
Wanna know why I've been lying to you?
Because of crap like this.

316
00:24:04,527 --> 00:24:06,194
-Like what?
-The way you talk to me.

317
00:24:06,362 --> 00:24:08,238
The way you look at me
like l'm a freak.

318
00:24:08,405 --> 00:24:10,406
-l do not.
-Even worse, like l'm an idiot.

319
00:24:10,574 --> 00:24:13,910
Like l don't know the difference
between right and wrong.

320
00:24:16,705 --> 00:24:17,747
What?

321
00:24:17,915 --> 00:24:20,917
Do you know the difference?
You've been strolling a dark road.

322
00:24:21,085 --> 00:24:23,253
You have no idea
what I'm going through. None.

323
00:24:23,420 --> 00:24:26,506
-Then enlighten me!
-l've got demon blood in me, Dean.

324
00:24:27,049 --> 00:24:29,050
This disease
pumping through my veins...

325
00:24:29,218 --> 00:24:32,095
...and l can't ever rip it out
or scrub it clean.

326
00:24:32,304 --> 00:24:35,348
I'm a whole new level of freak.

327
00:24:37,393 --> 00:24:41,563
And l'm just trying to take this curse...

328
00:24:41,730 --> 00:24:44,440
...and make something good out of it.

329
00:24:46,527 --> 00:24:47,610
Because I have to.

330
00:24:58,873 --> 00:25:00,874
Let's just go talk to the guy.

331
00:25:01,041 --> 00:25:03,126
I mean, Jack.

332
00:25:03,335 --> 00:25:05,253
Okay?

333
00:25:15,973 --> 00:25:17,765
Jack Montgomery?

334
00:25:19,268 --> 00:25:23,146
I'm Sam Winchester.
This is my brother, Dean.

335
00:25:23,355 --> 00:25:25,148
We need to talk.

336
00:25:30,112 --> 00:25:31,738
About?

337
00:25:32,364 --> 00:25:33,948
About you.

338
00:25:34,116 --> 00:25:35,450
About how you're changing.

339
00:25:36,952 --> 00:25:37,994
Excuse me?

340
00:25:38,162 --> 00:25:41,164
You're probably feeling your bones
move under your skin.

341
00:25:41,373 --> 00:25:44,459
Your appetite's reaching, you know,
Hungry, Hungry Hippo levels.

342
00:25:44,627 --> 00:25:45,960
How am l doing so far?

343
00:25:49,131 --> 00:25:50,590
Who the hell are you guys?

344
00:25:50,758 --> 00:25:53,009
We're people who know something
about something.

345
00:25:53,177 --> 00:25:55,136
We're people who can help.

346
00:25:55,763 --> 00:25:57,764
Please just hear us out.

347
00:26:01,101 --> 00:26:02,810
-A what?
DEAN: A Rougarou.

348
00:26:02,978 --> 00:26:06,606
Sounds made-up, I know,
but believe me, it's not.

349
00:26:06,774 --> 00:26:11,527
All right, l've noticed certain things.
I mean, some strange things.

350
00:26:11,695 --> 00:26:15,156
But l just-- I don't know.
I'm sick or something.

351
00:26:15,658 --> 00:26:17,408
Your father was one of these things.

352
00:26:20,537 --> 00:26:23,665
Your real father.
He passed it on to you.

353
00:26:27,002 --> 00:26:30,171
No. Are you guys listening to yourselves?
You sound like--

354
00:26:30,339 --> 00:26:34,717
Let's skip the whole "you guys sound
crazy," shall we? You're hungry, Jack.

355
00:26:34,927 --> 00:26:36,970
You're only gonna get hungrier.

356
00:26:37,137 --> 00:26:39,180
-Hungrier for...?
-Long pig.

357
00:26:39,848 --> 00:26:43,643
A little "Manburger Helper"
may have crossed your mind already.

358
00:26:46,063 --> 00:26:48,481
-No.
-lt doesn't have to be like this, Jack.

359
00:26:48,649 --> 00:26:50,525
-You can fight it off. Others have.
-No.

360
00:26:50,693 --> 00:26:52,735
We're not gonna lie.
It's not gonna be easy.

361
00:26:52,945 --> 00:26:55,655
You're gonna feel like an alcoholic
swimming in whiskey.

362
00:26:55,823 --> 00:26:59,492
But l'm telling you, you gotta say no.

363
00:27:00,369 --> 00:27:01,452
-Or--
-Or what?

364
00:27:02,037 --> 00:27:04,038
SAM:
You feed once, and it's all over.

365
00:27:05,374 --> 00:27:07,834
And then we'll have to stop you.

366
00:27:10,087 --> 00:27:11,754
Stop me?

367
00:27:12,881 --> 00:27:16,217
My dad, did somebody stop him?

368
00:27:17,720 --> 00:27:18,970
Yes.

369
00:27:20,597 --> 00:27:24,559
Get off my property right now. I see
you guys again, I'm calling the cops.

370
00:27:24,727 --> 00:27:27,395
Jack, your wife, everybody you know,
they're in danger.

371
00:27:27,563 --> 00:27:29,480
Now!

372
00:27:35,779 --> 00:27:37,613
Good talk.

373
00:27:48,751 --> 00:27:52,253
MlCHELLE: Jack, I don't know where you
are, but you're scaring me. Come home.

374
00:27:52,421 --> 00:27:55,214
We need to talk. Please?

375
00:27:55,382 --> 00:27:56,549
[BEEP]

376
00:28:33,796 --> 00:28:36,422
Damn it, Jack, no.

377
00:28:37,341 --> 00:28:39,092
Come on.

378
00:29:14,086 --> 00:29:18,840
No.

379
00:29:21,718 --> 00:29:22,844
WOMAN:
Ah!

380
00:29:23,011 --> 00:29:25,888
-Wait! We're here to save you, l guess.
-l'm calling the police.

381
00:29:26,098 --> 00:29:28,015
-We should go.
-Yeah.

382
00:29:41,530 --> 00:29:44,031
Michelle, I'm home.

383
00:29:48,036 --> 00:29:49,704
Hey, babe?

384
00:29:50,497 --> 00:29:52,206
Are you here?

385
00:29:53,208 --> 00:29:54,542
[MUMBLlNG]

386
00:29:54,835 --> 00:30:21,652
Michelle.

387
00:30:22,154 --> 00:30:24,780
Okay, we're gonna stay calm.

388
00:30:24,948 --> 00:30:27,617
We're gonna give this man
whatever he wants.

389
00:30:27,784 --> 00:30:31,078
Okay? Anything.
Just take it and go, please.

390
00:30:31,246 --> 00:30:33,664
I'm sorry about this, Jack.

391
00:30:34,166 --> 00:30:35,958
I truly am.

392
00:30:36,877 --> 00:30:39,378
It's not the way that l wanted it to go.

393
00:30:39,546 --> 00:30:40,880
JACK:
Who are you?

394
00:30:42,090 --> 00:30:44,800
You already met some friends of mine.

395
00:30:45,427 --> 00:30:47,303
Two brothers.

396
00:30:47,471 --> 00:30:49,555
They said that if l--

397
00:30:50,682 --> 00:30:54,393
Look, l haven't hurt anybody.

398
00:30:54,561 --> 00:30:58,105
Not yet, but you would've.
They always do.

399
00:30:58,607 --> 00:31:01,484
-l'm doing you a favor, son.
-Jack, what's he talking about?

400
00:31:04,321 --> 00:31:06,322
Tell her, Jack.

401
00:31:06,490 --> 00:31:09,492
Tell her the truth.
She deserves to know.

402
00:31:11,703 --> 00:31:14,622
Just let her go.
She's not a part of this.

403
00:31:14,790 --> 00:31:16,457
A part of what?

404
00:31:18,126 --> 00:31:19,627
Jack?

405
00:31:19,795 --> 00:31:23,714
I really do apologize,
but she is part of it.

406
00:31:25,092 --> 00:31:26,634
What?

407
00:31:27,302 --> 00:31:29,136
TRAVlS:
Michelle.

408
00:31:29,304 --> 00:31:31,514
Tell him what you told me
when l got here.

409
00:31:34,768 --> 00:31:36,519
Michelle?

410
00:31:41,358 --> 00:31:45,653
I said, "Don't hurt me...

411
00:31:47,489 --> 00:31:50,241
...because I'm pregnant."

412
00:31:55,831 --> 00:31:59,292
-Just hold on a minute.
-Now you see the mess we're in?

413
00:31:59,459 --> 00:32:02,128
I can't make this mistake
all over again.

414
00:32:02,296 --> 00:32:05,006
I won't be around in 30 years.
This has got to end now.

415
00:32:06,675 --> 00:32:10,511
I know you don't believe me, but l'd
give anything not to have to do this.

416
00:32:10,679 --> 00:32:14,974
No. You don't-- No. No.

417
00:32:19,479 --> 00:32:22,398
-Oh, God. Please, no!
-You don't have to do this.

418
00:32:22,566 --> 00:32:27,069
If you wanna kill me, kill me,
but not my wife. Okay?

419
00:32:27,279 --> 00:32:29,280
-l'm begging you.
-Ain't got no choice.

420
00:32:31,867 --> 00:32:33,075
My condolences.

421
00:32:34,036 --> 00:32:35,286
No.

422
00:32:37,331 --> 00:32:38,998
Jack.

423
00:32:41,877 --> 00:32:43,044
[GRUNTlNG]

424
00:33:00,312 --> 00:33:01,395
Jack!

425
00:33:03,398 --> 00:33:04,899
Ah!

426
00:33:10,906 --> 00:33:12,239
[GRUNTlNG]

427
00:33:47,776 --> 00:33:48,943
[GASPS]

428
00:33:52,739 --> 00:33:55,157
-Stay away from me!
-Michelle.

429
00:34:46,418 --> 00:34:50,713
-l guess now we know where Travis is.
-That stupid son of a bitch.

430
00:35:19,868 --> 00:35:20,868
Oh, God.

431
00:35:22,329 --> 00:35:24,538
Think that's Travis?

432
00:35:25,373 --> 00:35:27,458
What's left of him.

433
00:35:29,711 --> 00:35:31,712
Guess you were right about Jack.

434
00:35:33,340 --> 00:35:35,216
Dean!

435
00:36:04,704 --> 00:36:06,413
Dean?

436
00:36:07,415 --> 00:36:09,500
Dean can't come to the phone
right now.

437
00:36:10,252 --> 00:36:14,421
-Jack! lf you hurt him, I swear to God--
-Calm down!

438
00:36:15,799 --> 00:36:17,091
Your brother's alive.

439
00:36:18,385 --> 00:36:20,636
But not if you don't calm down.

440
00:36:21,221 --> 00:36:24,306
All right. Jack, listen.

441
00:36:24,516 --> 00:36:27,434
Open the door.
We can figure this out, okay?

442
00:36:27,602 --> 00:36:30,563
Oh, we'll have ourselves
a little brainstorming session.

443
00:36:30,730 --> 00:36:33,274
-Jack, please.
-l don't think so.

444
00:36:34,276 --> 00:36:37,903
-After what you did?
-What? What are you talking about?

445
00:36:39,114 --> 00:36:41,323
You send your friend here.

446
00:36:41,533 --> 00:36:45,077
He tried to burn my wife alive.

447
00:36:45,662 --> 00:36:47,788
What? Why?

448
00:36:53,628 --> 00:36:55,588
He didn't say.

449
00:36:57,966 --> 00:37:02,678
I guess psychopaths
don't know how to explain themselves.

450
00:37:04,055 --> 00:37:06,140
Listen to me. You gotta believe me.

451
00:37:06,641 --> 00:37:09,810
My brother and l,
we never would've hurt her, okay?

452
00:37:20,071 --> 00:37:23,824
-Oh, God, l'm so hungry.
-Jack, don't do this.

453
00:37:25,327 --> 00:37:28,203
I can't ever see my family again.

454
00:37:31,958 --> 00:37:33,626
You two.

455
00:37:33,793 --> 00:37:37,379
-Your friend. You made me into this!
-No one's making you kill us.

456
00:37:41,718 --> 00:37:45,304
Listen to me. You got this dark pit
inside you, I know.

457
00:37:45,472 --> 00:37:47,014
Believe me, l know.

458
00:37:47,182 --> 00:37:49,892
But that doesn't mean
you have to fall into it.

459
00:37:50,101 --> 00:37:51,602
You don't have to be a monster.

460
00:37:53,897 --> 00:37:57,399
-Have you seen me lately?
-lt doesn't matter what you are.

461
00:37:57,609 --> 00:37:59,193
It only matters what you do.

462
00:38:02,530 --> 00:38:04,698
It's your choice.

463
00:38:08,870 --> 00:38:11,121
[GRUNTlNG]

464
00:38:26,221 --> 00:38:27,888
Jack!

465
00:38:39,234 --> 00:38:41,360
[JACK SCREAMlNG]

466
00:39:14,811 --> 00:39:17,021
You did the right thing, you know.

467
00:39:17,605 --> 00:39:20,607
That guy was a monster.
There was no going back.

468
00:39:26,031 --> 00:39:29,158
I wanna tell you l'm sorry.
I've been kind of hard on you lately.

469
00:39:29,325 --> 00:39:30,826
Don't worry about it, Dean.

470
00:39:34,497 --> 00:39:37,916
It's just that your psychic thing,
it scares the crap out of me.

471
00:39:38,084 --> 00:39:42,337
Look, if it's all the same,
I'd really rather not talk about it.

472
00:39:44,799 --> 00:39:47,092
What? You don't wanna talk? You?

473
00:39:47,260 --> 00:39:50,471
There's nothing more to say.
I can't keep explaining myself to you.

474
00:39:50,638 --> 00:39:53,140
I can't make you understand.
Well, why don't you try?

475
00:39:53,308 --> 00:39:56,769
I can't, because this thing,
this blood...

476
00:39:56,936 --> 00:40:00,314
...it's not in you the way it's in me.

477
00:40:00,482 --> 00:40:02,316
It's just something l gotta deal with.

478
00:40:04,277 --> 00:40:05,319
Not alone.

479
00:40:12,494 --> 00:40:14,828
Anyway, it doesn't matter.

480
00:40:15,371 --> 00:40:17,331
These powers...

481
00:40:18,291 --> 00:40:20,542
...it's playing with fire.

482
00:40:21,920 --> 00:40:23,003
I'm done with them.

483
00:40:25,006 --> 00:40:26,924
I'm done with everything.

484
00:40:27,425 --> 00:40:28,801
Really?

485
00:40:30,428 --> 00:40:33,472
Well, that's a relief. Thank you.

486
00:40:33,640 --> 00:40:35,599
Don't thank me.
I'm not doing it for you.

487
00:40:36,267 --> 00:40:39,228
Or for the angels, or for anybody.

488
00:40:40,814 --> 00:40:43,065
This is my choice.

489
00:41:20,436 --> 00:41:22,437
[ENGLISH SDH]

